;; smoke-trap.expected.sexp — guest expectation document, converted from smoke-trap.expected.toml by
;; scripts/convert_dossier.py (SOT-FORMAT.4). One document form; validate with
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py smoke-trap.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp
;; Round-trip: `python3 scripts/convert_dossier.py verify smoke-trap.expected.toml smoke-trap.expected.sexp` — data-equal, comment census exact.

(comment "smoke-trap.expected.toml — expected observations for `smoke-trap.s`." "" "The expected observation here is a TRAP, not a value, which is the whole reason this program" "exists: `G0` requires the evidence path to carry a failure case, because a model that computes" "correctly and misreports faults is invisible to arithmetic-only differential testing.")
(expectations (program "smoke-trap.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 3) (never_written "x1") (step (n 0) (insn "addi x10, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x10") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "Building the main-memory base arithmetically; LUI cannot produce a positive 0x8000_0000.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn "slli x10, x10, 31") (writes (write (reg "x10") (value "0x0000000080000000"))) (derivation "1 << 31 at 64 bits is the base of the declared MainMemory region.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1")) (step (n 2) (insn "lw x1, x10, 1025") (writes) (derivation "The effective address is 0x80000000 + 1025 = 0x80000401, which is NOT 4-byte aligned. This profile does not handle misaligned accesses invisibly, so the access raises an address-misaligned exception delivered as a contained trap. ⭐ x1 is therefore NEVER WRITTEN — a model that quietly serviced the misaligned load would write it, which is the negative observation that distinguishes the two behaviours. Observed on both references as cause 0x04 with tval = 0x0000000080000401.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.6 (the EEI defines whether misaligned accesses are handled invisibly) — decision D-MISALIGN-DATA")))
